betalm: LG G8S ThinQ (SM8150) board, keys, Synaptics S3706 touch, A640 GPU

sweet_board.h gains sweet_board_betalm() (ADT root compatible "lge,betalm";
the ADT keeps "xiaomi,sweet" too, as raphael does) and sweet_board_sm8150()
(raphael or betalm). The SM8150-common paths that 0260-0262 gated on
raphael now take sweet_board_sm8150(): volume-up on PM8150 GPIO6 (SID 0
0xc500, as in the LGE sm8150-beta DT), the PM8150 RTC and its alarm-data
offset, IORTC, the SPMI read/write allow-lists, and the PM8150B FG gen4
battery poll (design capacity 3550 mAh on the G8S).

GPU: gpu_board_a640_betalm (same SM8150 blocks as raphael). Its cmd-db
address is 0 = read the base from AOP message RAM (0x0c3f000c), as
ios-sweet betalm 0090 / ios-flame do on this phone, instead of raphael's
fixed 0x85f20000. Zap carve-out pil_gpu_region 0x99915000 (G8S live DT,
after LG's dtbo; ios-sweet betalm 0094).

sweet_touch.c: a fourth touch board. Synaptics S3706 (RMI4) at 0x20 on
qupv3_se17_i2c = wrapper 2 SE0 @0xc80000, SDA/SCL GPIO 55/56 function 1,
reset 54, ATTN 122, rails as TLMM enables vdd 152 / vcl 59, all in the
SOUTH tile (0x03d00000). GCC vote 0x52014 bits 0-4, RCG 0x1e148, branch
0x1e144 (ios-sweet betalm 0085, verified on the phone with xnu-8796).
LG's QUP firmware runs SE17 GSI-only, so the existing bit-banged I2C is
used (~200 kHz, sweettouchbb=2), reads paced by the ATTN edge latch and
limited to the first 2 object slots (sweettouchfingers=N). RMI4: PDT scan,
F01 setup (normal, configured, nosleep, all IRQs), F12 register-descriptor
parsing, polled objects. sweettouchflip=N: bit0 mirror x, bit1 mirror y,
bit2 swap. A SiW SW42000 at 0x28 is detected and reported as unsupported.
The sweet, beryllium and raphael boards are unchanged.

